{
  "title": [
    "Notice people take a small step back",
    "mid-conversation, even hours after your shower?",
    "Foods That Make Body Odor Worse"
  ],
  "eyebrow": "Body Odor Alert",
  "cover_char_file": "마늘기름_illust.jpg",
  "char_display_names": {
    "마늘기름_illust.jpg": "Garlic & Onion",
    "소고기_illust.jpg": "Red Meat",
    "맥주_illust.jpg": "Alcohol"
  },
  "items": [
    {
      "name": "Why this happens",
      "char_file": "마늘기름_illust.jpg",
      "body": [
        "Body odor forms when food",
        "compounds are released",
        "through sweat and breath",
        "",
        "Some foods make far more",
        "of these odor molecules"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Garlic & Onion",
      "char_file": "마늘기름_illust.jpg",
      "body": [
        "Sulfur compounds like allicin",
        "can keep releasing through",
        "sweat and breath",
        "",
        "For over 24 hours",
        "after you eat them"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Garlic & Onion — the fix",
      "char_file": "마늘기름_illust.jpg",
      "body": [
        "Cook them instead",
        "of eating raw"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Red Meat",
      "char_file": "소고기_illust.jpg",
      "body": [
        "Beef takes longer",
        "to digest than",
        "other proteins",
        "",
        "That slower breakdown makes",
        "more odor-causing compounds"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Red Meat — the fix",
      "char_file": "소고기_illust.jpg",
      "body": [
        "Swap it for white fish",
        "or chicken breast sometimes"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Alcohol",
      "char_file": "맥주_illust.jpg",
      "body": [
        "Beer and wine break down",
        "into acetic acid,",
        "released through sweat",
        "",
        "Often giving a sour,",
        "vinegar-like edge"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Alcohol — the fix",
      "char_file": "맥주_illust.jpg",
      "body": [
        "Drink water",
        "alongside it"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "closing": {
    "headline": [
      [
        "You don't have to",
        "cut these out completely"
      ],
      [
        "Cooking and swapping",
        "a few things helps"
      ]
    ],
    "tip": [
      "Fresh vegetables and herbs",
      "on the side can help too"
    ],
